      "Daemon Records is always sending me new releases, or at least it seems that way. Don't get me wrong, I'm not complaining, I am more bragging, :). Three Finger Cowboy is a four piece from the southeast. They are so indie sounding. I love it. I mean, it sounds like it was recorded the entire CD in one day. The guitars are not polished, and the vocals are very dry, but Katharine Mcelroy has such a pretty voice, and it really shines past everything. At certain points I am reminded of the Stockton, California band Pavement. On \"Never Did You Ever\" you can hear the dragging drums, and the simple guitar melody. I always say simple is good. Check out A Foot Of Snow (In the Sound booth). it's worth your time to go pick this one up. Atmospheric, free flowing, relaxing, and very visual. That is how I would describe Chicago's The Timeout Drawer. This disc is full go great melody, and emotion. Ever since I received this disc, I have been listing to it. I was so impressed, that I contacted there record company (Some Odd Pilot) and requested that they send me a couple more copies. Space Rock, meets ambient emo. The songs are driving, and catchy. I have never herd anything like The Timeout Drawer before. I believe this is Some Odd Pilots first release, let's hope they find us more great acts like this. Get this disc ! (Check out there website too, it's worth your time.) Three Finger Cowboy is a four piece from the southeast. They are so indie sounding. I love it. I mean, it sounds like it was recorded the entire CD in one day. The guitars are not polished, and the vocals are very dry, but Katharine Mcelroy has such a pretty voice, and it really shines past everything. At certain points I am reminded of the Stockton, California band Pavement. On \"Never Did You Ever\" you can hear the dragging drums, and the simple guitar melody. I always say simple is good. Check out A Foot Of Snow (In the Sound booth). it's worth your time to go pick this one up."
